<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berber Dahir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1930</span> · Also known as Berber Decree</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> Dahir was a decree issued on 16 May 1930 in the name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-v-of-adal">Sultan Muhammad V</a> under the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a>. It placed Berber-speaking areas under customary law administered by local councils and French criminal courts rather than Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharia">sharia</a> courts. Seen as an attempt to divide Berbers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> and weaken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, it provoked widespread protest and helped launch the Moroccan nationalist movement.</p></div>
